@model VeSessionManager.Core.Entities.User?
@*
    The nudge for admin accounts without two-factor (#356).

    Enforcement was considered and deliberately not built: this deployment's system SMTP has
    historically not been configured, so an admin who loses a phone cannot necessarily be emailed a
    way back in — and the account that would rescue them is the one that would be locked. So the
    door stays open and this is loud instead.

    Shown only to SystemAdmin and TeamAdmin: those are the accounts that read candidate personal
    data and hold team credentials. Showing it to every role would make it wallpaper, and wallpaper
    is not a nudge.

    Not dismissible, on purpose. A dismissed nudge is a nudge that stops working the moment it is
    inconvenient, and the only way to make it go away — turning 2FA on — is the point.
*@
@if (Model is { } user
    && !user.TwoFactorEnabled
    && user.Role is VeSessionManager.Core.Entities.UserRole.SystemAdmin
        or VeSessionManager.Core.Entities.UserRole.TeamAdmin)
{
    <div class="twofactor-nudge">
        <i class="bi bi-shield-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i>
        <span>
            <strong>Two-factor authentication is off.</strong>
            Strongly recommended for an account that can read candidate personal data.
        </span>
        <span class="spacer"></span>
        <a class="btn-secondary btn-sm" asp-page="/Account/TwoFactor">Set it up</a>
    </div>
}
